Dark mode now covers the pagination. The cause was a single hardcoded light color, not a missing theme: the shared pager painted its strip with literal `#F8FAFC`, so in dark mode the buttons switched to dark tokens while the strip behind them stayed white — exactly what your screenshot shows.

What changed:

- [PaginationBar.svelte](frontend/src/components/common/PaginationBar.svelte) — `.pagination-shell` background now uses `var(--z-surface-2)`, which is `#f8fafc` in light and `#132042` in dark, so every page using the shared pager follows the theme.
- [IndexPageLayout.svelte](frontend/src/lib/components/index/IndexPageLayout.svelte) — the index footer's pager override had the same `#F8FAFC` literal; it now uses the same token so nested index pages can't re-introduce a light strip.
- [PaginationBar.svelte](frontend/src/components/common/PaginationBar.svelte#L264) — in dark mode the global `html.dark [class*='label']` rule was inheriting the page text color, so «نمایش / ردیف» and the count label rendered as bright as the numbers; they're now pinned to the muted token.

Verified against the running dev server: in dark mode the strip resolves to `rgb(19, 32, 66)`, arrows to `#0f1a35` with `#1e2c4f` borders, the active page to brand blue, the size group to `#1a2848` with a `#0f1a35` active chip, and labels to the muted `#8a96b8`. In light mode the same elements still resolve to `#f8fafc` / white / `#64748b`, matching the reference, so the light design is untouched. `src/design-system.test.js` (52 tests) passes after the change, and this is the pager on the products page in dark mode:

![Pagination in dark mode](reports/pagination-dark.png)

Not covered: the older Bootstrap `pagination pagination-circle` pagers still used by some legacy pages (apartments, hospital, inventory records). They already have `html.dark .pagination .page-link` overrides in `app.css`, but I couldn't load a page with rows to eyeball those, so I'm not claiming they were visually checked.
